{"name":"Yarrow","hex":"#d8ad39","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Yarrow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in Lancashire, England, which flows into the River Douglas.","A river, named Yarrow Water, in Scottish Borders council area, Scotland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Yarrow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Achillea millefolium","blocks":[{"text":"Achillea millefolium, commonly known as yarrow or common yarrow, is a flowering plant in the family Asteraceae. Growing to 1 metre tall, it is characterized by small whitish flowers, a tall stem of fernlike leaves, and a pungent odor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg/330px-Achillea_millefolium_%28bright%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Achillea_millefolium","wikidata":"Q25408"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/02_Achillea_sp..jpg/500px-02_Achillea_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/02_Achillea_sp..jpg/500px-02_Achillea_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Achillea sp.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A02_Achillea_sp..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/03_Achillea_sp..jpg/500px-03_Achillea_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/03_Achillea_sp..jpg/1280px-03_Achillea_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/03_Achillea_sp..jpg/500px-03_Achillea_sp..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Achillea sp. in a heart sha